{
  "_info": "Devices and LED commands read on 2026-11-21 from the VPC profiles in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\VIRPIL\\PROFILES and the connected USB devices. LED command = the Tag value in the OUTPUT section of the profile (05-24 = LEDs on the board). The names led01, led02 ... follow the numbering in VPC Configuration Tool. On cp2 (Control Panel #2) the aliases were tested against the panel on 2026-11-21: b1-b10 = buttons B1-B10, gear_left/gear_nose/gear_right = the three round LEDs below the gear symbol, ind_* = the small indicators. All devices were mapped against the real panels with photos on 2026-11-21: cp1 and cp1_l (Control Panel #1, left and right) b1-b12 = buttons B1-B12; sharka b1-b8, rst, dir = the buttons with those labels; throttle (MongoosT-50CM3) b1-b6 = buttons B1-B6. Use Setup in the control panel to find or rename LEDs. Brightness: Virpil only has the levels 0, 64, 128 and 255 per colour channel; other values are rounded. The indicators use 128 (medium) or 64 (dim); gearred (gear moving) uses 255 (full). 'startup' is the base colour each LED shows when no rule or API call says otherwise; on_disconnect_color and on_exit = 'startup' make the LEDs return to it when MSFS closes or the bridge quits.",
  "vpc_led_control": {
    "exe": "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\VPC Software Suite\\tools\\VPC_LED_Control.exe",
    "command_template": "\"{exe}\" {vid} {pid} {cmd} {r} {g} {b}"
  },
